  "name": "Property taxes: capping the growth",
  "blurb": "Ohio homeowners saw large property tax increases after recent reappraisals. A citizen campaign to abolish property taxes in the state constitution did not collect enough valid signatures and is not on the November 2026 ballot. In late 2025 lawmakers passed a package that limits how fast some property taxes can grow instead. Supporters call it the biggest property tax change in decades; opponents in both parties said it does too little for homeowners, or that it moves too fast and leaves schools and local governments to sort out the effects.",
